<title>USA: Hanover Dir Q1 shr loss $0.05 vs loss $0.10.</title>
<headline>Hanover Dir Q1 shr loss $0.05 vs loss $0.10.</headline>
<dateline>WEEHAWKEN, N.J. 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hanover Direct Inc</p>
<p>				 Consolidated Operating Summary</p>
<p>			    13 weeks ended:</p>
<p>			 March 29,		  March 30,</p>
<p>			  1997			  1996</p>
<p> Shr		 loss $0.05	     loss $0.10</p>
<p> Net		 loss $6,621	    loss $9,477</p>
<p> Revs		129,725		   165,527</p>
<p> Avg shrs	  144,647,898	    93,493,937</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTES: Hanover attributes most of the decrease in total revenues to decrease in sales from discontinued catalogs.</p>
<p>Revenues from continuing catalogs dropped 6.8 percent to $122.6 million from $131.6 million a year ago. The company said the drop is due to reduction in circulation to only high-profit customers.</p>
</text>
